From c18eed1940f6a0e552215dc24477fa4a885963a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:28:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 67/94] ASoC: codecs: hiby-hm100: native DSD

Play native DSD on the analog outputs the way stock's hiby_snd_hw_params
does: a DSD_U32 FE (bit-interleaved to 16-bit words by q6asm-dai) gets
the DSD design ("mdsd") or, in "dsd" mode, the PCM design, pcm_dsd_sel
set and the DSD rate word (mode 2) for DSD64 to DSD512, with stock's
first-play kick and its dsd_compensate volume term. A design is only
reloaded when the other one is in SRAM, after muting synchronously
(including the SoC-side LO/BAL-LO mutes, which hold while the FPGA has
no design), and an output switch with a DSD stream open brings the DSD
design back. A failed reload leaves the target off. The DSD formats
never take a spdif_table word. Add "DSD Compensate" and "DSD Mode"
controls with stock's defaults.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
---
